From 75364fdc67605d7e6c5dec95cdaff4298f86ba40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codebuff <noreply@codebuff.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 19:46:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] qb64pe: exit programs cleanly on Haiku instead of crashing on
 END

Haiku's libglut registers an exit handler that destroys the remaining GLUT
windows and calls BGLView::UnlockGL() on them. QB64 terminates a program from
the main loop thread while the window belongs to the thread inside
glutMainLoop(), so that unlock hits Haiku's "UnlockGL called without LockGL"
debugger() and every program died with a crash report after a normal END.

The runtime now goes through QB64_QUIT(), which on Haiku flushes and calls
_exit() so the exit handlers never run; every other platform keeps plain
exit(). All terminating exit() calls in libqb.cpp are routed through it.
---
 qb64pe/internal/c/libqb.cpp | 98 ++++++++++++++++++++++---------------
 1 file changed, 58 insertions(+), 40 deletions(-)

diff --git a/qb64pe/internal/c/libqb.cpp b/qb64pe/internal/c/libqb.cpp
index d2a4defba..773d57d2d 100644
